{
  "user_id": 4,
  "reason": "Account shows locked with 5 failed logins; check for suspicious activity given malware email in quarantine"
}

{
  "summary": "User Tom Becker (Finance, user_id 4) asked us to release a quarantined \"scanned document zip\" that he believes came from the office copier. Quarantine shows Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", received 2026-10-08 08:52 UTC, reason MALWARE, releasable=false. The sender is an external domain, not an internal copier, and this matches a common fake-scanner malware lure. I did NOT release it (policy/KB-008). User says it's legitimate, so passing to security to review and confirm. Also noticed: the account is locked after 5 failed password attempts on 2026-10-09 between 10:12 and 10:27 ET, all from the usual corporate IP 203.0.113.10. No hosting-network or foreign sign-ins; past 14 days of successful sign-ins are normal and used Duo. Looks like the user mistyping, but given the lure, please confirm. User hasn't asked for an unlock and I didn't queue one. Needed: security review of Q-1005 and the sender domain, a check on whether other users got it, and an unlock or reset once the user is verified if needed. Unrelated: Q-1004 (Harborview invoice, spam) is also in quarantine and can be released if the user says he expects it.",
  "reason": "User wants a malware-flagged message released and believes it is legitimate (KB-007 escalation criterion); security must review."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found the email you mean, \"Scanned document 0931.zip\". Our filter flagged it as malware, so I can't release it. It came from an outside address (scanner@docs-share.example), not our office copier, and fake 'scanned document' emails are a common way attackers send malicious files. I've sent it to our security team to review. Please don't try to get the file another way, and don't open any similar zip attachments. If you need the scan, rescan it at the copier, or ask the person who scanned it to resend it or save it to a shared folder. Also, your account is locked after several wrong password attempts this morning. If you need it unlocked or your password reset, reply here or call the help desk. There's also a quarantined invoice from Harborview Supplies. Let me know if you're expecting it and I'll ask to have it released.",
  "internal_note": "Checked the quarantine. Q-1005 is from scanner@docs-share.example, subject 'Scanned document 0931.zip', reason malware, releasable=false. Not released, per KB-007/KB-008. The sender is an external domain, not an internal copier, so this looks like a scan-themed malware lure. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation id 1). The account is locked after 5 failed_password attempts on 10/09 between 10:12 and 10:27 ET, all from the usual corporate IP. Sign-in history otherwise looks normal, with Duo on all successes and no hosting or foreign IPs. The user didn't ask for an unlock, so none was queued. Q-1004 (Harborview invoice, spam, releasable) is also in quarantine; release it only if the user confirms he expects it.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
